  "question": {
    "text": "A current-carrying wire is placed in the grooves of an insulating semicircular disc of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, as shown. The current enters at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and leaves from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. Determine the magnetic field at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0032889_Question.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 124px;\" />",
